From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shelley Vohr <shelley.vohr@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 17:29:19 +0000
Subject: PipeWire capturer: keep the persist mode with the restore token

BaseCapturerPipeWire always asks the ScreenCast portal for
persist_mode "transient" and remembers the token it gets back in
RestoreTokenManager under the capturer's SourceId, so that a second
capturer selecting that SourceId reopens the session without another
portal dialog. The persist mode is not remembered, so a token that was
issued as "persistent" is restored with "transient". xdg-desktop-portal
drops the stored grant when a token is used and saves it again with
the persist mode of that request, so the grant moves from the
permission store into memory and no longer survives a restart of the
application. An embedder that wants to keep the user's choice across
launches, which ScreenCast version 4 supports, has no way to get or
keep a persistent token through this capturer.

Store the persist mode next to the token in RestoreTokenManager and
have Start() request the stored mode when it restores an entry, so a
persistent token stays persistent. AddToken() defaults to kTransient,
which is what the capturer records for tokens it obtained itself, so
current callers behave as before. AddToken() also now replaces an
existing entry instead of insert()ing, which kept the first token for
a SourceId. The ScreenCast documentation makes restore tokens single
use and says to continue with the one Start returns.
xdg-desktop-portal 1.18 returns the same string, so keeping the first
one has not mattered there.

The enum moves from ScreenCastPortal to
modules/portal/screencast_persist_mode.h, with
ScreenCastPortal::PersistMode kept as an alias, so that
restore_token_manager.h does not have to include screencast_portal.h.

An embedder can seed an entry with kPersistent (and a token saved from
an earlier run, if it has one) under a SourceId, either a new one from
GetUnusedId() or the one a capturer reports in GetSourceList(), call
SelectSource() with it before Start(), and read the token back with
GetEntry() once the capture has started.

Tested on GNOME 46 with xdg-desktop-portal 1.18.4 (ScreenCast version
5). With a kPersistent entry the portal dialog is shown on the first
launch only, the token lands in the permission store, and later
launches restore the session without a dialog. Restoring that token
with kTransient instead, which is what the capturer did before this
change, returns the same token but removes it from the permission
store, and the next launch shows the dialog again. With no entry the
dialog is shown on every launch, as before.

Bug: webrtc:566241633

Backport of https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/505860.
This patch can be removed once that CL rolls into Chromium.

